/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 86 0 R
/T (The primary aim of this project is to develop an AI-based Malicious URL Detection System capable of accurately identifying whether a given URL is safe or malicious. With the rapid growth of internet usage and the increasing number of phishing attacks, fraudulent websites, and malware distribution, there is a growing need for an intelligent system that can detect harmful URLs before users access them.)
/E (The primary aim of this project is to develop an AI-based Malicious URL Detection System capable of accurately identifying whether a given URL is safe or malicious. With the rapid growth of internet usage and the increasing number of phishing attacks, fraudulent websites, and malware distribution, there is a growing need for an intelligent system that can detect harmful URLs before users access them.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 86 0 R
/T (The proposed system utilizes Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) and Machine Learning \(ML\) techniques to analyze various characteristics of a URL, such as its structure, length, domain-related features, and other relevant attributes. Based on these features, the trained model classifies the URL as either benign \(safe\) or malicious, enabling users to avoid potentially dangerous websites.)
/E (The proposed system utilizes Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) and Machine Learning \(ML\) techniques to analyze various characteristics of a URL, such as its structure, length, domain-related features, and other relevant attributes. Based on these features, the trained model classifies the URL as either benign \(safe\) or malicious, enabling users to avoid potentially dangerous websites.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 86 0 R
/T (Another important objective of this project is to improve the accuracy of malicious URL detection while minimizing false positives and false negatives. Unlike traditional blacklist-based approaches, which can only identify previously known malicious websites, the proposed AI model is capable of recognizing newly generated and previously unseen malicious URLs by learning patterns from historical data.)
/E (Another important objective of this project is to improve the accuracy of malicious URL detection while minimizing false positives and false negatives. Unlike traditional blacklist-based approaches, which can only identify previously known malicious websites, the proposed AI model is capable of recognizing newly generated and previously unseen malicious URLs by learning patterns from historical data.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
