/T (The rapid growth of the internet has transformed the way people communicate, conduct business, access information, and perform financial transactions. With the increasing dependence on online platforms for banking, shopping, education, and social networking, the number of internet users has grown significantly over the past decade. While this digital transformation has brought numerous benefits, it has also created new opportunities for cybercriminals to exploit users through various forms of cyberattacks.)
/E (The rapid growth of the internet has transformed the way people communicate, conduct business, access information, and perform financial transactions. With the increasing dependence on online platforms for banking, shopping, education, and social networking, the number of internet users has grown significantly over the past decade. While this digital transformation has brought numerous benefits, it has also created new opportunities for cybercriminals to exploit users through various forms of cyberattacks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 86 0 R
/T (Among the most common cyber threats are phishing attacks, where attackers create malicious websites that closely resemble legitimate websites to deceive users into revealing sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, banking credentials, credit card details, and personal information. These phishing websites are often designed to imitate trusted banking portals, e-commerce platforms, government services, and popular social media websites, making it difficult for users to distinguish between genuine and fraudulent websites.)
/E (Among the most common cyber threats are phishing attacks, where attackers create malicious websites that closely resemble legitimate websites to deceive users into revealing sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, banking credentials, credit card details, and personal information. These phishing websites are often designed to imitate trusted banking portals, e-commerce platforms, government services, and popular social media websites, making it difficult for users to distinguish between genuine and fraudulent websites.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 86 0 R
/T (In addition to phishing websites, cybercriminals also distribute malware through malicious URLs. When users unknowingly visit these websites, malware can be automatically downloaded onto their devices, leading to data theft, ransomware attacks, unauthorized access, and financial losses. As cyber threats continue to evolve, malicious websites are becoming more sophisticated and are capable of bypassing conventional security mechanisms.)
/E (In addition to phishing websites, cybercriminals also distribute malware through malicious URLs. When users unknowingly visit these websites, malware can be automatically downloaded onto their devices, leading to data theft, ransomware attacks, unauthorized access, and financial losses. As cyber threats continue to evolve, malicious websites are becoming more sophisticated and are capable of bypassing conventional security mechanisms.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
