/T (The working process of the proposed system begins when a user enters or submits a URL through the application's interface. The system first performs URL preprocessing, where the entered URL is cleaned and validated to ensure it is in the correct format. After preprocessing, the system extracts several important features from the URL, such as URL length, number of special characters, number of subdomains, presence of an IP address, use of HTTPS, domain-related information, and other lexical and structural characteristics. These extracted features serve as input for the machine learning model.)
/E (The working process of the proposed system begins when a user enters or submits a URL through the application's interface. The system first performs URL preprocessing, where the entered URL is cleaned and validated to ensure it is in the correct format. After preprocessing, the system extracts several important features from the URL, such as URL length, number of special characters, number of subdomains, presence of an IP address, use of HTTPS, domain-related information, and other lexical and structural characteristics. These extracted features serve as input for the machine learning model.)
