203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Traditional malicious URL detection methods primarily rely on blacklist-based systems, where known malicious websites are stored in a centralized database. Whenever a user attempts to access a website, the URL is compared against the blacklist. If the URL is present in the database, access is blocked or a warning is displayed. Although this approach is effective for detecting previously identified malicious websites, it has several significant limitations.)
/E (Traditional malicious URL detection methods primarily rely on blacklist-based systems, where known malicious websites are stored in a centralized database. Whenever a user attempts to access a website, the URL is compared against the blacklist. If the URL is present in the database, access is blocked or a warning is displayed. Although this approach is effective for detecting previously identified malicious websites, it has several significant limitations.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (One of the major drawbacks of blacklist-based detection is that it can identify only known malicious URLs. Cybercriminals frequently create new phishing websites and malicious domains that are not yet included in the blacklist. As a result, these newly generated websites can remain undetected and continue to deceive users until they are reported and added to the database.)
/E (One of the major drawbacks of blacklist-based detection is that it can identify only known malicious URLs. Cybercriminals frequently create new phishing websites and malicious domains that are not yet included in the blacklist. As a result, these newly generated websites can remain undetected and continue to deceive users until they are reported and added to the database.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Another limitation is the inability to detect zero-day phishing attacks. Since newly created malicious websites often remain active for only a short period before being replaced with new ones, traditional detection methods fail to provide adequate protection against these rapidly changing threats.)
/E (Another limitation is the inability to detect zero-day phishing attacks. Since newly created malicious websites often remain active for only a short period before being replaced with new ones, traditional detection methods fail to provide adequate protection against these rapidly changing threats.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Furthermore, manual updating of blacklist databases is both time-consuming and resource-intensive. Security organizations must continuously monitor suspicious websites, verify malicious activity, and regularly update their databases. This delay between the creation of a malicious website and its addition to the blacklist creates a window of opportunity for attackers to target a large number of users.)
/E (Furthermore, manual updating of blacklist databases is both time-consuming and resource-intensive. Security organizations must continuously monitor suspicious websites, verify malicious activity, and regularly update their databases. This delay between the creation of a malicious website and its addition to the blacklist creates a window of opportunity for attackers to target a large number of users.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Due to these limitations, traditional detection techniques are no longer sufficient to address the rapidly evolving landscape of cyber threats. Intelligent approaches based on Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning are therefore required to detect both known and previously unseen malicious URLs with greater accuracy and efficiency.)
/E (Due to these limitations, traditional detection techniques are no longer sufficient to address the rapidly evolving landscape of cyber threats. Intelligent approaches based on Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning are therefore required to detect both known and previously unseen malicious URLs with greater accuracy and efficiency.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13]
>>
