/T (The increasing number of phishing attacks, malicious websites, and cyber threats has created a strong need for intelligent and efficient URL detection systems. Traditional blacklist-based methods have limitations as they mainly depend on previously identified threats and may fail to detect newly created malicious websites. The proposed AI Malicious URL Detector addresses these challenges by using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning techniques to analyze URL patterns and classify websites based on their security level.)
/E (The increasing number of phishing attacks, malicious websites, and cyber threats has created a strong need for intelligent and efficient URL detection systems. Traditional blacklist-based methods have limitations as they mainly depend on previously identified threats and may fail to detect newly created malicious websites. The proposed AI Malicious URL Detector addresses these challenges by using Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning techniques to analyze URL patterns and classify websites based on their security level.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 100 0 R
/T (The integration of AI improves the accuracy and efficiency of malicious URL detection by enabling the system to learn from existing datasets and identify hidden patterns associated with cyber threats. Unlike conventional approaches, the proposed system can detect suspicious and previously unseen URLs by analyzing various URL features such as structure, length, domain characteristics, and other relevant attributes.)
/E (The integration of AI improves the accuracy and efficiency of malicious URL detection by enabling the system to learn from existing datasets and identify hidden patterns associated with cyber threats. Unlike conventional approaches, the proposed system can detect suspicious and previously unseen URLs by analyzing various URL features such as structure, length, domain characteristics, and other relevant attributes.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
