858 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Data Flow Diagram \(DFD\) illustrates how data moves through the AI Malicious URL Detector system. The process begins when the user submits a URL through the web interface. The URL is then preprocessed to remove unnecessary characters and normalize the input. Next, relevant features are extracted from the URL, including its length, number of subdomains, use of HTTPS, presence of special characters, and other lexical characteristics.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 633 0 R
/Next 859 0 R
>>
endobj
859 0 obj
<<
/Title (These extracted features are forwarded to the Machine Learning model, which analyzes the data and predicts whether the URL is Safe or Malicious. The prediction result is then displayed to the user. Additionally, the URL, prediction result, confidence score, and timestamp are stored in the database for future analysis and record keeping.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 633 0 R
/Prev 858 0 R
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Title (Technology)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 368 0 R
/Prev 634 0 R
/Next 861 0 R
>>
endobj
861 0 obj
<<
/Title (Purpose)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 368 0 R
/Prev 860 0 R
/First 947 0 R
/Last 948 0 R
/Count -24
/Next 635 0 R
>>
endobj
862 0 obj
<<
/Title (The proposed solution provides faster detection compared to traditional manual verification and blacklist-based approaches. By generating real-time predictions, it helps users identify potentially harmful websites before accessing them, thereby reducing the chances of phishing attacks, malware infections, financial fraud, and unauthorized access to sensitive information.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 31 0 R
/Prev 636 0 R
/Next 863 0 R
>>
endobj
863 0 obj
<<
/Title (The AI-based detection system can be further enhanced and expanded in the future by integrating it with browser extensions, email security systems, and enterprise-level cybersecurity solutions. Such integration can provide automatic protection while users browse websites, open emails, or access online services.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 31 0 R
/Prev 862 0 R
/Next 637 0 R
>>
endobj
