1081 0 obj
<<
/Title (Among the most common cyber threats are phishing attacks, where attackers create malicious websites that closely resemble legitimate websites to deceive users into revealing sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, banking credentials, credit card details, and personal information. These phishing websites are often designed to imitate trusted banking portals, e-commerce platforms, government services, and popular social media websites, making it difficult for users to distinguish between genuine and fraudulent websites.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1027 0 R
/Prev 1073 0 R
/Next 1074 0 R
>>
endobj
1082 0 obj
<<
/Title (To overcome these challenges, Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) and Machine Learning \(ML\) have emerged as powerful solutions for malicious URL detection. Unlike traditional methods, AI-based systems learn patterns and characteristics from large datasets of both benign and malicious URLs. By analyzing various features such as URL length, domain structure, special characters, subdomains, and lexical patterns, machine learning models can accurately predict whether a URL is legitimate or malicious, even if it has never been encountered before.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1075 0 R
/Next 1088 0 R
>>
endobj
1083 0 obj
<<
/Title (After extracting these features, the processed data is provided as input to the machine learning model for training and classification. Effective feature extraction improves the ability of the AI model to distinguish between legitimate and malicious URLs, resulting in better detection accuracy and reduced false predictions. Thus, feature extraction acts as a bridge between raw URL data and the intelligent decision-making process of the proposed malicious URL detection system.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1089 0 R
/Next 1076 0 R
>>
endobj
1084 0 obj
<<
/Title (The machine learning model is the core component of the AI Malicious URL Detector responsible for analyzing extracted URL features and predicting whether a given URL is safe, suspicious, or malicious. The model is trained using a dataset containing examples of both legitimate and malicious URLs, allowing it to learn patterns and characteristics associated with different types of web threats.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1076 0 R
/Next 1090 0 R
>>
endobj
