/Title (The machine learning model is trained using publicly available datasets containing legitimate and malicious URLs collected from trusted sources such as cybersecurity research repositories and open-source datasets. These datasets are used solely for academic research, model training, testing, and performance evaluation. No personally identifiable information \(PII\) is included or processed during the development of the system.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1165 0 R
/Prev 1172 0 R
/Next 1183 0 R
>>
endobj
1178 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project also promotes the responsible use of Artificial Intelligence. The AI model is designed to assist users by providing risk predictions and should not be considered a replacement for professional cybersecurity solutions. Continuous evaluation, regular model updates, and unbiased training practices are essential to maintain accuracy, reduce false predictions, and ensure fair and reliable decision-making.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1165 0 R
/Prev 1183 0 R
/Next 1173 0 R
>>
endobj
1179 0 obj
<<
/Title (The proposed AI Malicious URL Detector is an intelligent web security system designed to identify malicious URLs using Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) and Machine Learning \(ML\) techniques. The system aims to provide real-time detection of phishing websites, malware distribution links, and other harmful URLs by analyzing their characteristics and classifying them as Safe, Suspicious, or Malicious.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1174 0 R
/Next 1184 0 R
>>
endobj
1180 0 obj
<<
/Title (The proposed solution offers several advantages, including real-time detection, improved accuracy, reduced dependence on blacklist databases, and the ability to detect newly created phishing websites. By integrating Artificial Intelligence with cybersecurity techniques, the system provides a reliable, scalable, and user-friendly approach for protecting users against modern web-based cyber threats.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1174 0 R
/Prev 1185 0 R
>>
endobj
